What the editor does in this example is simple: write out the new version of the ﬁle under temporary name (foot.txt.tmp), force it to disk with fsync(), and then, when the application is certain the new ﬁle metadata and contents are on the disk, rename the temporary ﬁle to the original ﬁle’s name.
This last step atomically swaps the new ﬁle into place, while concurrently deleting the old version of the ﬁle, and thus an atomic ﬁle update is achieved.

